# 2. Main objective

Implement browser-based push notifications that can:

- Appear in the browser notification panel.
- Reach users when the application is in the background.
- Reach users when the application tab is closed, subject to browser and operating-system support.
- Display notifications on the user's device even when they are not actively using the application.
- Open the relevant application page when clicked.
- Target a particular employee or administrator rather than broadcasting every event to everybody.

FCM must work alongside the existing persistent in-app notification system.

IMPORTANT:

Firestore in-app notifications and browser push notifications are two different delivery mechanisms.

Firestore remains the authoritative notification history.

FCM is the external browser/device delivery mechanism.

A notification event should first be recorded persistently and then delivered through FCM to the appropriate registered devices.

Do not replace the existing notification system with FCM.

