# 18. Duplicate prevention and delivery reliability

Avoid duplicate push notifications.

Use deterministic event IDs or idempotency keys.

One business event should create one logical notification per intended recipient.

A user with multiple registered devices may receive the same event on each active device, but the application should not create multiple in-app notification records merely because the user has multiple devices.

Handle:

- Duplicate API requests.
- Retried operations.
- Multiple backend processes.
- Token refresh.
- Invalid tokens.
- Partial multicast failures.
- FCM unavailable.
- Network errors.
- Expired or invalid registration tokens.

Persist the in-app notification before attempting push delivery.

Use a reliable retry strategy only where appropriate.

Do not create uncontrolled retry loops.

Do not let a failed push prevent the original task operation from succeeding.

Do not claim guaranteed delivery merely because Firebase accepted a send request.

